# .pii-allowlist — exact-match emails the PII/secret gate in ./check.sh is allowed to see.
#
# The gate greps content dirs for anything shaped like an email and FAILS on a hit.
# Synthetic / placeholder addresses used in docs, specs, and test fixtures live here so
# they don't trip the gate. One address per line; matching is exact (grep -xF), not prefix.
# Comment lines (leading #) and blank lines are ignored. Add ONLY addresses that are
# provably fake — never a real person's address.
alice@example.com
bob@example.com
user@example.com
noreply@anthropic.com
